    <text type="letter">
        <body>
            <div type="writingSession">
                <pb n="1"/>
                <opener>
                    <dateline><date when="1947-02-07">February 7,
                        1947</date>.</dateline><salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4919"
                            type="person">Dr. Humphreys</rs>:</salute>
                </opener>
                <p>I was very glad to hear that you have the application of <rs
                        ref="#tillich_person_id__4918" type="person">Dr. Josef Maier</rs> under
                    consideration for a teaching position in the Department of Modern Language of
                    your College.</p>
                <p>I have known <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4918" type="person">Dr. Maier</rs> for
                    many years. He has always impressed me as a very vigorous and earnest young
                    scholar well deserving of the interest of an institution of higher learning. His
                    knowledge in the field of German literature and philosophy is profound, indeed.
                    He has of course full control of the German language. I have had frequent
                    opportunity to learn of his genuine pedagogic qualities through our internal
                    scientific conference on German philosophy and the sociology of German
                    literature as well as from observing his contacts with students from Columbia
                    University. He is well able to express his ideas so as to make himself
                    understood by every one, and he possesses also the patience and particular
                    faculties expected of a good teacher. <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4918"
                        type="person">Dr. Maier</rs> is now lecturing at New York University.</p>
                <p>Personally I have always felt a great attachment for him, and I am absolutely
                    convinced that he will be liked by any group of teachers and students with whom
                    he may come in contact at your institution.</p>
                <closer>
                    <salute>Sincerely yours,</salute>
                    <signed>
                        <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person"> Paul
                        Tillich</rs><lb/>Professor at Union Theological Seminary, <rs
                            ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New York</rs> 27, <rs
                            ref="#tillich_place_id__865" type="place">N. Y.</rs></signed>
                </closer>

            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
